WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:04.609
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
for Bonus Game of Thrones because Charles

00:00:04.609 --> 00:00:07.420
Dance teased we hadn’t seen the last of
him, I wanted to talk about top 10 dead characters

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:18.830
we’d like to see come back.

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:23.150
George RR Martin has always been good about
teasing the potential to see old characters

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:25.900
again through flashbacks, resurrection and
reanimation.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:33.090
And just a reminder to any new people, World
of Ice and Fire is out at the end of the month.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:35.680
So when we get closer to that I’ll be randomly
giving away a couple of copies.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.040
So be sure to subscribe so you don’t miss
any of that stuff!

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.649
Here’s my Top 10 I’d like to see back,
and I’ll explain how I’d like them to

00:00:40.649 --> 00:00:41.649
come back.

00:00:41.649 --> 00:00:43.810
Careful for spoilers through season 4 on the
show.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:47.280
I’ll wait just a sec...okay, here we go.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.880
Number 10 - The Giants Killed in the sacking
of Castle Black as Wights

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.989
I feel like we all want to see some zombie
giants.

00:00:53.989 --> 00:00:57.750
The show didn’t make it very clear but the
giant that Grenn killed in the tunnel was

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:58.980
Mag the Mighty.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:02.600
Giants don’t have kings, but Mag was something
of a leader for their tribe.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:03.800
Mance Rayder says there’s only a couple
hundred of them left.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:10.079
The only other one we know about that has
a name is Wun Wun, who’s even bigger than

00:01:10.079 --> 00:01:11.079
Mag.

00:01:11.079 --> 00:01:19.259
There’s a chance he could appear in Season
5 now that the wildling army has been subdued

00:01:19.259 --> 00:01:20.639
by Stannis.

00:01:20.639 --> 00:01:25.130
9 - Renly coming back in Visions to haunt
Loras

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:27.310
We haven’t seen a lot of ghosts in the series.

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:28.680
Visions are the next closest thing.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:33.270
I just like the idea that Renly Haunts Loras.

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:36.569
The show is doing a little more with the character
than the books are.

00:01:36.569 --> 00:01:38.999
Here’s a picture of Finn Jones on the set
of season 5.

00:01:38.999 --> 00:01:42.040
They’ve been filming a lot of King’s Landing
scenes the past couple of weeks.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:43.279
Vision Renly doesn’t have to be a bad thing.

00:01:43.279 --> 00:01:44.439
Just like a dark passenger who visits Renly
in his dreams.

00:01:44.439 --> 00:01:48.130
We didn’t see a ton of Renly thanks to Melisandre,
but Renly in the books was even more nuts

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:49.299
about pageantry.

00:01:49.299 --> 00:01:56.189
So if he did haunt Loras’ dreams, it would
probably be with a never ending tourney.

00:01:56.189 --> 00:02:05.130
The way I think about Renly in the books is
that he was a theater geek with crazy amounts

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:06.299
of money.

00:02:06.299 --> 00:02:09.849
8 - Grenn the Giantslayer brought back as
a Wight

00:02:09.849 --> 00:02:12.200
They burned all the bodies after the sack
of Castle Black.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:13.739
So technically this is impossible.

00:02:13.739 --> 00:02:19.019
But Grenn dying in the tunnel was one of the
changes the show made to the book story.

00:02:19.019 --> 00:02:33.790
He started out as the asshole that was bullying
Samwell in season 1, one of the brothers that

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:35.430
Jon fought off.

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:41.950
By the wildling attack in season 4 though
he had matured a lot as a character and gladly

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:43.819
gave his life for the rest of the brotherhood.

00:02:43.819 --> 00:02:50.079
Thus we remember him as Grenn the Giantslayer.

00:02:50.079 --> 00:02:55.349
7 - Ygritte coming back to Jon Snow as a Vision

00:02:55.349 --> 00:03:00.000
Her body was also burned, so the only way
she can come back is as a vision or a flashback.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.430
But Jon just seems like the kind of character
who is constantly haunted by spirits.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:07.000
Least of all his parents.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.209
Both real and adoptive.

00:03:08.209 --> 00:03:13.340
So far Ygritte is one of the few guides he’s
had.

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:18.940
I feel like he learned just as much with her
in his short time north of the wall as he

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:28.269
did in all 16 or 17 years growing up in Winterfell.

00:03:28.269 --> 00:03:33.629
One of the reasons I encourage you all to
read the books is because you get to see inside

00:03:33.629 --> 00:03:34.629
his head.

00:03:34.629 --> 00:03:36.230
Particularly during Book 5.

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:40.510
I’d really like to see him conjure up Ygritte
as a way for his subconscious to manifest

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:41.840
itself and give him advice.

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:45.299
It would be like Jon telling himself he knows
nothing.

00:03:45.299 --> 00:03:49.030
6 - Khal Drogo as a flashback

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:52.440
I just want Jason Momoa back on the show being
crazy.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:56.829
He was burned too, so the only way he’s
coming back is in non-corporeal form.

00:03:56.829 --> 00:04:00.969
Daenerys looks like she’s staying put in
Meereen for the time being, but at some point

00:04:00.969 --> 00:04:02.629
she’s going to have to march an army somewhere.

00:04:02.629 --> 00:04:07.319
I’d like to see her conjure up Khal Drogo
as a way to reassure herself during her conquest.

00:04:07.319 --> 00:04:08.349
Khal Drogo as he was as a Warlord.

00:04:08.349 --> 00:04:14.379
We really only saw him in and around his wedding
and short journey to the western coastline.

00:04:14.379 --> 00:04:17.970
He became Khal because he was such a great
warlord.

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:21.509
So he’d probably have some pretty good advice
to give in battle.

00:04:21.509 --> 00:04:25.550
5 - Catelyn Stark reanimated by the Red God

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:27.620
I feel like this is obligatory.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:32.781
She’s not my favorite character I’d like
to see, but she still an important one in

00:04:32.781 --> 00:04:34.449
the greater scheme of the books.

00:04:34.449 --> 00:04:39.650
I’ll be interested to see how the show fills
that gap.

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:42.080
Like who will they give the big vengeance
arc to.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:47.460
I do think they dropped the character, but
that doesn’t mean they dropped the role

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:49.460
she serves in the narrative.

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:53.740
4 - The Mountain reanimated as a Golem for
Clegane Bowl

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:58.020
It was implied that Qyburn was getting his
frankenstein on in the season 4 finale.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:00.650
So I’d just like to see that taken to the
logical next step.

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:06.050
It seemed like the show wanted the Hound to
die too, but since we didn’t see it happen

00:05:06.050 --> 00:05:12.879
on screen it’s possible they could bring
him back.

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:17.139
For those that haven’t seen the Clegane
Bowl forum threads, it’s just the idea that

00:05:17.139 --> 00:05:22.699
circumstances could allow The Mountain and
The Hound to face off in a big epic battle.

00:05:22.699 --> 00:05:25.660
Like their own version of Oberyn Martell vs
The Mountain.

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:27.250
Except they just hack each other to pieces.

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:32.050
There are all kinds of theories, so maybe
I’ll talk more about Clegane Bowl in a future

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:33.660
video.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:38.090
3 - Tywin Lannister reanimated by the Red
God

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:41.629
Recently Charles Dance said that we had not
seen the last of Twyin.

00:05:41.629 --> 00:05:44.740
I don’t think that means he’s coming back
to life on the show.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:06:07.380
I just think we’ll see the funeral.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:11.479
New seasons of the show always pick up in
the moments right after the previous season’s

00:06:11.479 --> 00:06:12.479
finale.

00:06:12.479 --> 00:06:18.110
So they’ll just address what happens with
the body of the most powerful man in Westeros.

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:23.140
I’d really love to see his character brought
back by the red god.

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:28.610
He only had a bunch of poison, rotting insides
and a few holes in his chest.

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:32.050
It’s not like half his face had fallen off.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:41.550
It’s a lot of fun to see beloved characters
come back, but I think it’s just as awesome

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:43.139
to see crazy villains return.

00:06:43.139 --> 00:06:44.410
2 - Oberyn Martell reanimated

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:48.540
I’d actually like to see Oberyn brought
back as a headless reanimated corpse.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:51.050
Like the headless horseman from sleepy hollow.

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:53.000
Only he wields his spear.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:59.490
and finally, the number character I want to
see again is Robert Baratheon as a Flashback.

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:03.389
Just so we can see what he learned at the
battle of the Trident when he killed Rhaegar

00:07:03.389 --> 00:07:04.389
Targaryen.

00:07:04.389 --> 00:07:07.699
He was supposedly the only person to hear
his dying words.

00:07:07.699 --> 00:07:14.020
When Rhaegar died he supposedly whispered
someone’s name.

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:19.449
I think it was Lyanna Stark, but Martin hasn’t
given any explicit information about that.

00:07:19.449 --> 00:07:23.091
He did say we would get more Robert’s Rebellion
flashbacks in the future books though.

00:07:23.091 --> 00:07:26.030
So we will learn what actually happened.

00:07:26.030 --> 00:07:29.990
Let me know though, which confirmed dead character
do you want to see again and how do you want

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:30.990
the show or the books to bring them back.

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:34.189
Remember, there’s a lot of literary devices
for bringing people back.

00:07:34.189 --> 00:07:40.409
Just as a bonus, I would like to see Flashbacks
for The Mad King and Rhaegar Targaryen, but

00:07:40.409 --> 00:07:44.250
I think sometimes it’s better that they
don’t do those things just so my imagination

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:45.470
can fill in the gaps.

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:49.330
That’s why reading the books can be more
fun at times, you just get the chance to imagine

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:53.330
something so much crazier than what they’re
capable of doing on the show.

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:57.289
Speaking of which, congratulations to this
week’s giveaway winner i love popcorn.

00:07:57.289 --> 00:07:58.590
I’ll reach out to you on your channel for
details.

00:07:58.590 --> 00:08:03.659
A lot of people die each year but I’ve already
done a video about one potential ending for

00:08:03.659 --> 00:08:04.659
the series.

00:08:04.659 --> 00:08:13.900
You can click here to learn more about that
and click here for more of my season 5 predictions.

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:16.500
A lot of stuff changing from the books.

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:19.309
Thanks for watching, everybody high five and
I’ll see you tonight for Gotham!

